        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5ffa7799ec204a68bde588b1525b203f",
      "statement": "A Claim carries absolute 0-based half-open char_start and char_end offsets in the original answer string (same convention as Citation offsets), a text field, a source_span back-reference to the AnswerSpan it came from, and a claim_index within that span.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/claims.py#L16-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b6e21c443655d1410bc4a705b11326c9b4b783c5e92d2bf5e2d3b5c766503f9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8163351d769940eaa92ed1bf02da33d2",
      "statement": "FactVerificationConfig is a frozen Pydantic model with verified_coverage_threshold (default 0.6, matching the default supported_answer_coverage so verify_facts and align_citations line up), partial_coverage_threshold (default 0.3), and an optional citation_config forwarded into each per-claim align_citations call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/fact_verification.py#L120-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be010b756238b461a64113ca91de24115f31abb9493b5acf25612ffa7326c3d5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/fact_verification.py#L27-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e56abac4c0d00136af708ffad26c69b48d1ad0cdb048815989213d9416c5c766:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3241e7c6e97a4bb2837f71086994b574",
      "statement": "When citation_config is not provided, verify_facts builds a CitationConfig with top_k=3, min_answer_coverage=0.2, and supported_answer_coverage=cfg.verified_coverage_threshold, so the per-claim \"supported\"/\"partial\"/\"unsupported\" semantics of align_citations line up with verify_facts's \"verified\"/\"partial\"/\"unverified\" rollup at the default threshold.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/fact_verification.py#L120-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be010b756238b461a64113ca91de24115f31abb9493b5acf25612ffa7326c3d5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c6cbc59f1704b988ad3d272934df554",
      "statement": "Each claim's status is derived from the per-claim align_citations run: the best Citation is the one with the highest score; if its answer_coverage is at least verified_coverage_threshold the status is \"verified\", at least partial_coverage_threshold the status is \"partial\", otherwise \"unverified\"; if align_citations returns no citations at all the status is \"unverified\" with confidence 0.0 and empty source_ids.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/fact_verification.py#L236-L290",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7db46c412892e68636dc9ceb4a84454b52c13bf475358a403da1586ae7fe06ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8f8c1eb8b5246a597c2b3016df526e1",
      "statement": "ClaimVerification.confidence is the best Citation's answer_coverage component (a coverage number in the alignment-pipeline sense, not a calibrated probability), and source_ids is the deduplicated set of source_id values across all_citations for that claim.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/fact_verification.py#L271-L289",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd937e25482a68e111ab994f2e369469c08f4292cb3b9ac955d47e0a588d7a36:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/fact_verification.py#L46-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b2f35b32a6ab1c178defc47c29b95ed35083eebad1984a9afea572f6e9a28b5a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e95be8c4d6574394a03e5ad899d684f7",
      "statement": "FactVerificationMetrics exposes num_claims, num_verified, num_partial, num_unverified, verification_rate, avg_confidence, min_confidence, a per-claim claim_verifications list in decomposition order, and the partitioned verified_claims, partial_claims, and unverified_claims Claim lists.",
